<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # How I Am Successful – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> My Personal Success Story</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> How I Am Successful</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Narrate a personal experience with learning a skill. Interactive: Engage in role-plays about navigating new environments.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can narrate a personal experience of learning a valuable skill (e.g., "Learning to manage my finances has helped me save for my higher education.")<br>Can answer questions about skill development experiences (e.g., "What was the most challenging part of managing finances?" "The most challenging part of learning to manage my finances was creating a budget that I could stick to.")<br>Can write a reflective essay on a personal experience with saving or managing money, connecting it to future goals or aspirations (e.g., "Learning to budget my allowance has taught me discipline and patience. If I keep saving consistently, I will be able to afford paying my university tuition next year, which will help me become more independent.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; width: 35%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; width: 45%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; width: 20%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification. This stage activates prior knowledge and sets the context for the lesson's speaking focus.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays images of successful young adults engaging in various activities (e.g., presenting a project, volunteering, saving money, learning a new skill). Students work in pairs to discuss: "What qualities do these people demonstrate? How have they achieved their success?" (5 min)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models answering one of the questions, emphasizing the use of Present Perfect and relevant vocabulary. For example: "This student <b>has demonstrated great initiative</b> by starting a community service project. They <b>have built a strong network</b> of volunteers, which <b>has been essential</b> for their growth." The teacher highlights content word stress (e.g., INITIATIVE, COMMUNITY SERVICE, STRONG NETWORK) and reduces stress on auxiliary verbs (həv, həs). (3 min)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'initiative,' am I talking about waiting for someone to tell you what to do, or taking action yourself?" (Expected answer: Taking action yourself.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is 'community service' something you do for yourself, or for your neighborhood and society?" (Expected answer: For the neighborhood/society.)</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Teacher prompts students to repeat key phrases with correct stress. (2 min)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: center;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "My Personal Success Story". This stage provides a model for narrative speaking.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> An authentic short audio recording (1-2 minutes) or a video clip of a young Panamanian entrepreneur narrating their personal experience of learning a valuable skill (e.g., managing a small business, mastering a digital skill for a project, or successfully saving for an investment). The genre is a personal narrative/interview snippet, focusing on their journey and challenges. (5 min)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Expressing personal experiences and aspirations for future growth.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students listen for gist: "What valuable skill has the speaker learned? What was their main achievement related to this skill?" (Students share answers orally in pairs).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">True/False statements (orally answered after a second listen): "The speaker has never faced any financial challenges." (False) "They will be managing their own company in five years if they continue their studies." (True, if stated).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Teacher monitors and facilitates oral discussion of answers. (5 min)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: center;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking. Students practice using target grammar and vocabulary in controlled and semi-controlled speaking activities.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice narrating personal experiences and expressing future goals using:
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar:</b> Present perfect for achievements ("I have saved...", "I have completed..."), Future continuous for long-term goals ("I will be managing...", "I will be pursuing..."), First conditional for future success ("If I continue..., I will find...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary:</b> success, goals, finances, savings, investment, career, growth, initiative, achievements, opportunities, strategies, future; save, complete, manage, invest, build, broaden, volunteer, pursue, participate, support, work, achieve, aspire, succeed, reflect, continue, lead, improve, contribute, initiate; successful, positive, professional, essential, significant, impactful, financial, careful, long-term, future-oriented, involved, collaborative, personal.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation:</b> Stressing content words and reducing stress on auxiliary verbs for natural rhythm.</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice: Sentence Completion & Partner Share (5 min)</b>
                        <br>Teacher provides sentence stems on the board or handout for students to complete orally in pairs, focusing on target grammar and vocabulary. Example stems:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 2px; text-align: justify;">"I have recently ______ (verb: complete, initiate) a project related to ______ (noun: community service, finances)."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 2px; text-align: justify;">"If I ______ (verb: continue, invest) my time in this skill, I will ______ (verb: achieve, broaden) more ______ (noun: opportunities, growth)."</li>
                        </ul>
                        <br>Students take turns completing the sentences and sharing them with their partner, paying attention to content word stress as modeled.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice: Structured Interview Questions (5 min)</b>
                        <br>Students work in new pairs. Teacher distributes cards with scaffolded interview questions. Partner A asks questions to Partner B, then they switch roles. Questions encourage use of target language:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 2px; text-align: justify;">"What valuable skill <b>have you learned</b> recently that contributes to your personal <b>growth</b>?" (Expected answer uses Present Perfect).</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 2px; text-align: justify;">"How <b>will you be managing your finances</b> in the next five years to achieve your <b>long-term goals</b>?" (Expected answer uses Future Continuous).</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 2px; text-align: justify;">"<b>If you continue to pursue</b> this career path, what kind of <b>impact will you be making</b>?" (Expected answer uses First Conditional and Future Continuous).</li>
                        </ul>
                        <br>Teacher reminds students to use appropriate intonation and stress.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Collaborative Dialogue: Peer Check & Expansion (5 min)</b>
                        <br>Still in pairs, students review their answers from the previous activity. They help each other refine their sentences for accuracy and fluency. They then challenge each other to expand on one answer by adding more details, using at least two new vocabulary words. (e.g., "That's a great answer! Can you tell me more about the *strategies* you'll use for that *investment*?") Teacher circulates, providing feedback on language use and pronunciation.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: center;">15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "My Personal Success Story". Focus on fluency and collaborative interaction.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Role-play: "Future Career Fair Interview". Students work in pairs. One student acts as a "Career Fair Recruiter" and the other as a "Prospective Candidate." The candidate must narrate their personal experience with learning a valuable skill, discussing past achievements, present efforts, and future goals, connecting them to potential career opportunities. The recruiter asks follow-up questions to delve deeper into the candidate's "success story." (10 min)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Theme/Scenario:</b> The role-play directly addresses "My Personal Success Story" by having students articulate how they are successful through skill development and future aspirations. It integrates "How I Am Successful" by requiring them to reflect on their own journey.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency, collaborative interaction, and communicative task completion. Students are encouraged to use the Present Perfect, Future Continuous, and First Conditional structures naturally, along with the target vocabulary. They should also respectfully discuss personal achievements and engage in conversations on goals and aspirations, as per pragmatic functions. (5 min for preparation, 5 min for role-play, then switch roles for 5 min).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Teacher circulates, listening for overall communication, fluency, and appropriate use of language. The goal is communication over perfect accuracy at this stage.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: center;">15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy to check speaking skills and content integration.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist for speaking performance. The teacher will focus on a few pairs at a time during the role-play, using a simple checklist to note student performance. (3 min for wrap-up)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students perform their "Career Fair Interview" role-play in pairs. The teacher selects 2-3 pairs to briefly present a portion of their dialogue to the whole class, or simply observes during the activity. (3 min)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation (content word stress clear).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of at least two target grammar structures (Present Perfect, Future Continuous, First Conditional).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Incorporation of at least three target vocabulary words.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and coherence in narrating the personal experience and discussing future goals.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Active listening and collaborative interaction with partner.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete the following prompts individually:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new skill-related vocabulary word I used successfully today was..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One thing I still find challenging when talking about my future goals is..."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: center;">6 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Opportunity for students and teacher to reflect on the learning process and plan next steps.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection Prompts (Oral discussion or quick write):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How has practicing narrating your success story today helped you articulate your personal achievements and future aspirations more clearly?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What specific strategies can you use to improve your spoken fluency when discussing complex topics like finances or career growth?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in promoting speaking fluency and accuracy using the target grammar and vocabulary? (e.g., The structured interview questions in Stage 3 effectively encouraged the use of specific tenses for speaking.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next speaking-focused activity or for students who struggled? (e.g., Some students still hesitate with auxiliary verb reduction; perhaps more specific drilling or listening practice for this next time. Maybe provide more sentence starters for lower-proficiency students in the production stage.)</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 4, students will transition from speaking about their personal success stories to writing about them. They will use the vocabulary, grammar, and ideas developed today to compose a reflective essay on a personal experience with saving or managing money, linking it to future goals, thereby building on their oral narrative skills for written production.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; text-align: center;">4 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>